,"name_hint":"api · 评审"},{"path":".agents/agents/reidbaker-agent/skills/code-documentation/SKILL.md","name":"code-documentation","description":"Guide for writing effective code documentation, including docstrings, JSDoc, dartdoc, and implementation comments. Use this skill when writing new code, adding features, or improving existing documentation in Dart, Python, or TypeScript to ensure clarity and maintainability.","headings":["Code Documentation Skill","1. General Philosophy","2. General Structure","3. Writing Guidelines","Brevity & Style","Formatting","4. Implementation Comments","5. Review Checklist","6. Language Specific Instructions"],"name_hint":"代码 · documentation"},{"path":".agents/agents/reidbaker-agent/skills/code-review/SKILL.md","name":"code-review","description":"Performs a comprehensive, multi-step code review of pull requests or local code changes, using iterative refinement (generation, critique, synthesis) to ensure high-quality, actionable feedback. Use when you need to review code changes thoroughly.","headings":["Comprehensive Code Review","Core Principles","Workflow","Step 1: Gather Changes","Step 2: Context Enrichment","Step 3: Generate Initial Review","Step 4: Critique and Refine (Review the Review)","Step 5: Synthesis (Final Review)","Output Format"],"name_hint":"代码 · 评审"},{"path":".agents/agents/reidbaker-agent/skills/grill-with-docs/SKILL.md","name":"grill-with-docs","description":"Grilling session that challenges your plan against the existing domain model, sharpens terminology, and updates documentation (CONTEXT.md, ADRs) inline as decisions crystallise. Use when user wants to stress-test a plan against their project's language and documented decisions.","headings":["Domain awareness","File structure","During the session","Challenge against the glossary","Sharpen fuzzy language","Discuss concrete scenarios","Cross-reference with code","Update CONTEXT.md inline","Offer ADRs sparingly"],"name_hint":"grill · with · 文档","description_zh":"对照项目现有领域模型、术语和已记录决策压力测试计划，在决策明确时同步更新 CONTEXT.md 和 ADR。"},{"path":".agents/agents/reidbaker-agent/skills/natural-writing/SKILL.md","name":"natural-writing","description":"Contains well-defined rules for creating natural, accurate, and readable writing. Use whenever authoring longer text, like analysis documents, PR or CL descriptions, or documentation.","headings":["Rules for Natural Writing","1. Vocabulary & Phrasing Controls","The \"Banned\" List","Avoid \"Copula\" Substitutions","Eliminate \"Elegant Variation\"","Banned Temporal Words in Code & Comments","2. Content & Tone","No \"Puffery\" or Forced Significance","No Superficial Analysis","Avoid Promotional Language","No \"Challenges and Future Outlook\" Formula","No \"Title as Proper Noun\" Leads","No Generic \"See Also\" Links","Attribution Precision","3. Sentence Structure","No Negative Parallelism","No \"Rule of Three\"","No False Ranges"],"name_hint":"natural · writing"},{"path":".agents/agents/reidbaker-agent/skills/unix-cli-best-practices/SKILL.md","name":"unix-cli-best-practices","description":"Safe, portable, and efficient command-line patterns for macOS/BSD Unix tools (grep, find, sed, awk, xargs, mdfind, pbcopy, open) and modern alternatives (ripgrep, fd). Covers common shell scripting and one-liner use cases including fast searching, text processing, codebase navigation, and parallel execution.","headings":["Unix CLI best practices","Modern high-performance alternatives","ripgrep (`rg`)","fd","Built-in tools for macOS and BSD","Efficient searching with grep","Slow: reads binary and ignored files","Fast: skips the directory completely at the filesystem level","High-performance traversal with find","Slow: traverses node_modules entirely, then filters output","Fast: skips node_modules entirely","macOS portability with sed","Edit in-place without creating a backup","Edit in-place and create a backup named filename.txt.bak","Codebase analysis with awk","Safe pipelines and parallelism with xargs","Unsafe: will fail or perform unintended actions if filenames contain spaces","Safe: handles spaces and special characters correctly"],"name_hint":"unix · cli · best · practices"},{"path":"skills/dart-add-unit-test/SKILL.md","name":"dart-add-unit-test","description":"Write and organize unit tests for functions, methods, and classes using `package:test`. Use when creating new logic or fixing bugs to ensure code remains correct and regression-free.","headings":["Testing Dart and Flutter Applications","Contents","Structuring Test Files","Writing Tests","Executing Tests","Test Implementation Workflow","Task Progress","Examples","Standard Unit Test Suite","Mocking with Mockito"],"name_hint":"dart · add · unit · 测试"},{"path":"skills/dart-build-cli-app/SKILL.md","name":"dart-build-cli-app","description":"Architectural patterns, entrypoint structure, exit codes, stream routing, and subprocess spawning for Dart command-line interface (CLI) applications. Use when building CLI tools, console utilities, scripts, argument parsing with `package:args` (ArgParser or CommandRunner), handling exit codes, configuring executables in pubspec.yaml, spawning Dart subprocesses, or compiling native CLI binaries. Don't use for Flutter UI widgets, web applications, or standalone HTTP backend servers.","headings":["Building Dart CLI Applications","Contents","1. Core Architecture & Process Lifecycle","Avoid Destructive Exits (`exit(N)`)","The Thin Entrypoint Pattern (`bin/` vs. `lib/src/`)","2. Output, Diagnostics & Formatting","3. Project Configuration & Packaging","Scaffolding & Pubspec Executable Mapping (`executables:`)","Single-Source Versioning (`package:build_version`)","Caching Conventions","4. Argument Parsing & Command Routing","5. Native Async & Modern Stack Traces","6. Subprocess Spawning & AOT Resilience","7. Signal Handling & Terminal Teardown","8. Testing CLI Applications","9. Modern Compilation & Distribution","10. Workflows & Audit Checklist","Implementation Workflow"],"name_hint":"dart · 构建 · cli · app"},{"path":"skills/dart-collect-coverage/SKILL.md","name":"dart-collect-coverage","description":"Collect coverage using the coverage packge and create an LCOV report","headings":["Implementing Dart and Flutter Test Coverage","Contents","Testing Fundamentals","Coverage Directives","Workflow: Configuring and Generating Coverage Reports","1. Add Dependencies","2. Collect Coverage and Generate LCOV","3. Feedback Loop: Validate Output","Workflow: Advanced Manual Coverage Collection","1. Run Tests with VM Service","2. Collect Raw Coverage","3. Format to LCOV","Examples","Example: `pubspec.yaml` Configuration","Example: Applying Ignore Directives"],"name_hint":"dart · collect · coverage"},{"path":"skills/dart-fix-runtime-errors/SKILL.md","name":"dart-fix-runtime-errors","description":"Uses get_runtime_errors and lsp to fetch an active stack trace, locate the failing line, apply a fix, and verify resolution via hot_reload.","headings":["Resolving Dart Static Analysis Errors","Contents","Core Concepts & Guidelines","Type System & Soundness","Null Safety","Error Handling","Workflows","Workflow: Static Analysis Resolution","Preview changes","Apply changes","Examples","Example: Fixing Dynamic List Assignments","Example: Fixing Method Overrides (Contravariance)","Example: Fixing Null Safety with `late`"],"name_hint":"dart · 修复 · runtime · errors"},{"path":"skills/dart-generate-test-mocks/SKILL.md","name":"dart-generate-test-mocks","description":"Define and generate mock objects for external dependencies using `package:mockito` and `build_runner`. Use when unit testing classes that depend on complex external services like APIs or databases.","headings":["Testing and Mocking Dart Applications","Contents","Structuring Code for Testability","Managing Dependencies","Generating Mocks","Implementing Unit Tests","Workflow: Creating and Running Mocked Tests","Task Progress","Feedback Loop: Test Failures","Examples","High-Fidelity Mocking and Testing Example"],"name_hint":"dart · 生成 · 测试 · mocks"},{"path":"skills/dart-migrate-to-checks-package/SKILL.md","name":"dart-migrate-to-checks-package","description":"Replace the usage of `expect` and similar functions from `package:matcher`\nto `package:checks` equivalents.","headings":["Migrating Dart Tests to Package Checks","Contents","When to Use This Skill","How to Use This Skill (The Workflow)","1. Dependency Setup","2. Identify and Plan Target Files","3. Migrating a File (Incremental or Full)","4. Verification and Feedback Loops","Key Syntax Differences and Pitfalls","1. Collection Equality Pitfall (`equals` vs `deepEquals`)","2. The `reason` Parameter is now `because`","3. Regular Expression Matching (`matches` vs `matchesPattern`)","4. Property Extraction (`TypeMatcher.having` vs `.has`)","5. Synchronous vs. Asynchronous `throws`","6. RegExp / Pattern Equality","7. Strict Nullable Boolean Safety (`bool?` fields)","8. Map Key Containment (`containsKey` vs `contains`)","9. Explicit Generic Parameters for Extension Types"],"name_hint":"dart · migrate · to · 检查 · package"},{"path":"skills/dart-resolve-package-conflicts/SKILL.md","name":"dart-resolve-package-conflicts","description":"Workflow for fixing package version conflicts. Use this when `pub get` fails due to incompatible package versions.","headings":["Managing Dart Dependencies","Contents","Core Concepts","Version Constraints","Workflow: Auditing Dependencies","Workflow: Upgrading Dependencies","Workflow: Resolving Version Conflicts","Examples","Tightening Constraints","Surgical Lockfile Removal"],"name_hint":"dart · resolve · package · conflicts"},{"path":"skills/dart-run-static-analysis/SKILL.md","name":"dart-run-static-analysis","description":"Execute `dart analyze` to identify warnings and errors, and use `dart fix --apply` to automatically resolve mechanical lint issues. Use during development to ensure code quality and before committing changes.","headings":["Analyzing and Fixing Dart Code","Contents","Analysis Configuration","Diagnostic Suppression","Workflow: Executing Static Analysis","Workflow: Applying Automated Fixes","Examples","Comprehensive `analysis_options.yaml`","Inline Diagnostic Suppression"],"name_hint":"dart · run · static · 分析"},{"path":"skills/dart-setup-ffi-assets/SKILL.md","name":"dart-setup-ffi-assets","description":"Guides agents in compiling and packaging C/C++ source code into dynamic or static libraries (Code Assets) using Dart's Native Assets hook system (via hook/build.dart and hook/link.dart utilizing package:hooks and package:native_toolchain_c). Use when a user asks to: 'setup native assets', 'compile C/C++ source code', 'bundle dynamic libraries', 'build native C code', 'link native assets', 'implement build.dart or link.dart hooks', or 'integrate C/C++ interop in Dart/Flutter'. Helps agents avoid manual toolchain orchestration and configures secure hash-validated binary downloads or advanced linker tree-shaking with package:record_use mapping.","headings":["Compiling C Code into Code Assets with Native Assets Hooks","Contents","Introduction","Constraints","Native Interop Packages","Step-by-Step Workflow","Step 1: Add Dependencies","Step 2: Define C Specifications","Step 3: Implement Build and Link Hook Scripts","Step 4: Run the Hook Cycle","Choosing an Integration Approach","Method 1: Local Compilation with Linker Tree-Shaking (Recommended)","Prerequisite Host Compiler Toolchains","C Source and Bindings Setup","Defining the C Library Build Spec","Implementing `hook/build.dart`","Implementing `hook/link.dart`","Method 2: Downloading Precompiled Dynamic Libraries"],"name_hint":"dart · 设置 · ffi · assets"},{"path":"skills/dart-use-doc-examples/SKILL.md","name":"dart-use-doc-examples","description":"How to inject external code examples into Dartdoc using the {@example} directive, and how to filter those files using #hide, #region, and #endregion tags.","headings":["Using Examples in Dartdoc","Contents","1. The `{@example}` Directive","2. Using Regions","3. Hiding Setup Code","4. Marker Filtering Rules","5. Placement and Path Resolution","6. Verification"],"name_hint":"dart · use · doc · examples"},{"path":"skills/dart-use-ffigen/SKILL.md","name":"dart-use-ffigen","description":"Guide agents to use `package:ffigen` to automatically generate FFI bindings instead of writing them manually. Use this skill when a task involves writing new FFI bindings, extending C/Objective-C/Swift integrations, or replacing hand-crafted `dart:ffi` setups.","headings":["Generating FFI Bindings using package:ffigen","Contents","Introduction","Constraints","FFIgen Overview","1. `FfiGenerator`","2. `Headers`","3. `Functions`","4. `Output`","Step-by-Step Workflow","Step 1: Check/Add Dependencies","Step 2: Formulate Paths Dynamically","Step 3: Write the Script (`tool/ffigen.dart`)","Step 4: Run Code Generation","Step 5: Static Analysis","Concrete Example: Binding a C Library","The C Header File (`third_party/sqlite/sqlite3.h`)","BEFORE: Manual FFI Binding (The Anti-Pattern)"],"name_hint":"dart · use · ffigen"},{"path":"skills/dart-use-path-package/SKILL.md","name":"dart-use-path-package","description":"Cross-platform file and directory path manipulation, segment splitting, extension extraction, and context conversion using `package:path` and `package:file`. Use when writing, inspecting, joining, splitting, or refactoring file paths, directory names, or extensions, or replacing raw string path operations (`.split('/')`, `'$dir/$file'`, `.endsWith('.ext')`, `.replaceAll('\\\\', '/')`). Don't use for HTTP network URI routing, database query strings, or non-path string processing.","headings":["Safe Cross-Platform Path Manipulation in Dart","Contents","1. Core Principles & Cross-Platform Rules","Avoid Treating File Paths as Raw Strings","Pragmatic Boundary Joining vs. Multi-Segment Decomposition (`p.join`)","Normalization vs. Canonicalization (`p.normalize` vs. `p.canonicalize`)","Strip Location Specifiers & Convert URIs Safely","2. Recommended package:path Idioms vs. String Anti-Patterns","Path Joining","Segment Matching","Root and Directory Prefixes","File Extensions","Extension Slicing and Compound Extensions","POSIX and URL Path Conversion","URI Conversion","Directory Basename Helper","3. Bridging Native Paths to POSIX, Git, & URL Contexts","Git Paths and Repository Metadata"],"name_hint":"dart · use · path · package"},{"path":"skills/dart-use-pattern-matching/SKILL.md","name":"dart-use-pattern-matching","description":"Applies Dart 3 pattern matching, switch expressions, and destructuring idiomatically to validate data schemas, handle algebraic data types, and decompose control flow. Use when refactoring complex if-else chains, parsing polymorphic JSON or API responses, destructuring Records or Maps, or enforcing exhaustiveness on sealed classes. Don't use for simple boolean conditions, single-variable type promotion (use `is`), or basic collection filtering.","headings":["Implementing Dart Patterns","Contents","Pattern Selection Strategy","Switch Statements vs. Expressions","Core Pattern Implementations","Pragmatic Balance & Anti-Patterns","1. Prefer `is` Type Promotion over `if-case` for Single Promotable Variables","2. Consolidate Nullable Types in Switch Arms","3. Preserve Fast-Fail Validation (Do Not Silently Drop Data)","4. Avoid Single-Case or Boolean Switches","5. Avoid Gratuitous Object Destructuring","6. Avoid `if-case` for Standalone Scalar Comparisons","Workflows","Task Progress: Implementing Pattern Matching","Feedback Loop 1: Exhaustiveness Checking (Static Verification)","Feedback Loop 2: Runtime Map & JSON Pattern Verification","Examples","Polymorphic JSON Deserialization (Discriminated Unions)"],"name_hint":"dart · use · pattern · matching"},{"path":"skills/dart-use-primary-constructors/SKILL.md","name":"dart-use-primary-constructors","description":"Help users write syntactically and semantically correct primary constructors in Dart, and migrate/use the new constructor syntax, empty-body semicolon syntax, in-body initializer list syntax, and abbreviated concise constructor syntax.","headings":["Dart Primary Constructors & New Constructor Syntax Skill","Dart Version Requirements","1. Overview","Key Benefits","2. Syntax Reference","2.1 Basic Class Header Syntax","2.2 Declaring, Initializing, and Plain Parameters","2.3 Constant Primary Constructors","2.4 Extension Types","2.5 Empty Body Semicolon Shorthand (`;`)","2.6 The In-Body Part of a Primary Constructor (`this ...`)","2.7 Abbreviated Concise Constructor Syntax","3. Semantics & Scoping Rules","3.1 Primary Initializer Scope","3.2 Late Instance Variables Restriction","3.3 Shadowing","3.4 Generative Constructor Restrictions","3.5 Parameter Mutation Errors"],"name_hint":"dart · use · primary · constructors"},{"path":"skills/dart-write-documentation/SKILL.md","name":"dart-write-documentation","description":"Rules and formatting guidelines for writing Dart /// API documentation and doc comments. Use when documenting Dart code, writing doc comments for any Dart declaration (libraries, classes, methods, variables, etc.), or when instructed to follow the Effective Dart documentation guidelines.","headings":["Writing Dart API Documentation","Contents","1. Scope and Structure","2. Tone and Openers","3. Strict Anti-Patterns (Banned)","4. Technical Placement & Resolution","5. Linking and Markdown","6. Verification","Examples","1. Banned Tags vs. Prose","2. The Annotation Placement Trap","3. Openers and Tone","4. Constructor Linking","5. Out-of-Scope Links (@docImport)"],"name_hint":"dart · 编写 · documentation"},{"path":"skills/flutter-add-integration-test/SKILL.md","name":"flutter-add-integration-test","description":"Configures Flutter Driver for app interaction and converts MCP actions into permanent integration tests. Use when adding integration testing to a project, exploring UI components via MCP, or automating user flows with the integration_test package.","headings":["Implementing Flutter Integration Tests","Co